# Whitespace hygiene

After every code edit, scan changed files for excessive vertical whitespace before finishing.

## Rules

- **At most one blank line** between statements, properties, imports, or JSX/Svelte blocks.
- **No blank lines** immediately after `{`, `(`, `[`, or opening tags — or immediately before `}`, `)`, `]`, or closing tags.
- **At most two blank lines** between top-level sections (e.g. import block → code, or logical groups in long files).
- **Trim trailing whitespace** on edited lines.
- **No blank lines at EOF** — files end with a single newline.

## Common AI mistakes

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — double/triple blank lines between every line
import { foo } from './foo';


const bar = 1;


function baz() {


  return bar;


}

// ✅ GOOD — single blank line between logical groups only
import { foo } from './foo';

const bar = 1;

function baz() {
  return bar;
}
```

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<script>


  let count = $state(0);


</script>


<div>


  {count}


</div>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<script>
  let count = $state(0);
</script>

<div>
  {count}
</div>
```

## Workflow

1. After editing, re-read the diff or changed regions.
2. Collapse runs of 2+ consecutive blank lines down to 0–1 as appropriate.
3. Do not reformat unrelated parts of the file — only fix whitespace in edited regions unless the whole file is clearly broken.
